-- title:
--   Reduction is regular at ordinary points jmath̃=a with a^{q^2}=a
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $f$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the coefficientwise base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$. Assume the Laurent series underlying $f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with $j$ and $j_q$ at the prime complement of the reduction kernel, that its image $\pi f$ under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by the mod-$q$ reductions of $j$ and $j_1$, and that $\pi f \neq 0$. Let $a \in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2} = a$ and $a \notin$ `ssJSet q k`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic Weierstrass models over $k$ have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Assume finally that no place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $W.\mathrm{ord}(f) \neq 0$ admits simultaneously $x \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}(x) = a$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j - x) > 0$, and $y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}(y) = a^q$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q - y) > 0$, where $j$ and $j_q$ denote the images in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` of the $q$-expansions `jq` and `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`. Then the order of $\pi f$ at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a`, the place of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` transported from the place $X - a$ of $k(X)$, is zero.
--
--   This is the ordinary, $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-rational case of the statement that a function on $X_0(q)$ whose $q$-expansion is integral and localisable has a reduction with neither zero nor pole at a non-supersingular point $\tilde\jmath = a$ of the special fibre, provided $f$ itself has no zero or pole specialising to the point $(a, a^q)$ of the Kronecker congruence. It is one of the two branches combined in [`ModularCurve.ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero_of_not_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero_of_not_mem_ssJSet), the branches being separated by whether $a$ is fixed by the square of the Frobenius.
